  "vo": "Same thousand bucks in cash. Six decades. What did inflation eat? Opened today. Only the year you stuffed it changes. 2016? It buys twenty-eight percent less. Three envelopes, gone. 2006? Thirty-nine percent less. Four. 1996? Fifty-three percent. Half the pile, gone. 1986? Sixty-seven percent. Seven envelopes. 1976? Eighty-three. Eight envelopes. And 1966? Ninety percent. Nine of ten envelopes, eaten. Prices are ten times higher. So your grand buys a hundred. And the envelope still holds the…",
